# Retrieving Interfaces from a GraphQL Endpoint

There are several ways to discover interfaces in a GraphQL schema:

## 1. **Introspection Query**

GraphQL has a built-in introspection system. You can query it directly:

```graphql
# Get all interfaces
{
  __schema {
    types {
      name
      kind
      description
      fields {
        name
        type {
          name
        }
      }
      possibleTypes {
        name
      }
    }
  }
}
```

To filter **only interfaces**:

```graphql
{
  __schema {
    types(filter: { kind: INTERFACE }) {
      name
      kind
      fields {
        name
        type {
          name
          kind
        }
      }
      possibleTypes {
        name
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Or query a **specific type** to check if it implements interfaces:

```graphql
{
  __type(name: "YourTypeName") {
    name
    kind
    interfaces {
      name
      description
    }
  }
}
```

## 2. **Using `curl` or HTTP Client**

```bash
curl -X POST https://your-api.com/graphql \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "query": "{ __schema { types { name kind possibleTypes { name } } } }"
  }'
```

Then filter results where `kind === "INTERFACE"`.

## 3. **Using JavaScript/Fetch**

```javascript
const query = `
{
  __schema {
    types {
      name
      kind
      fields {
        name
      }
      possibleTypes {
        name
      }
    }
  }
}`;

const response = await fetch('https://your-api.com/graphql', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ query })
});

const { data } = await response.json();

// Filter only interfaces
const interfaces = data.__schema.types.filter(t => t.kind === 'INTERFACE');
console.log(interfaces);
```

## 4. **Using GraphQL Tools/IDEs**

| Tool | How |
|------|-----|
| **GraphiQL** | Use the "Docs" sidebar panel to browse interfaces |
| **Apollo Studio** | Schema explorer shows interfaces visually |
| **Postman** | Auto-generates schema docs from introspection |
| **Insomnia** | Built-in schema explorer |
| **Altair** | Docs panel + autocomplete |

## 5. **Full Introspection Query (Standard)**

The standard full introspection query used by most tools:

```graphql
query IntrospectionQuery {
  __schema {
    queryType { name }
    mutationType { name }
    types {
      ...FullType
    }
  }
}

fragment FullType on __Type {
  kind
  name
  description
  fields(includeDeprecated: true) {
    name
    args { name type { ...TypeRef } }
    type { ...TypeRef }
    isDeprecated
    deprecationReason
  }
  interfaces { ...TypeRef }
  possibleTypes { ...TypeRef }
  enumValues(includeDeprecated: true) { name }
}

fragment TypeRef on __Type {
  kind
  name
  ofType {
    kind
    name
    ofType {
      kind
      name
    }
  }
}
```

## ⚠️ Important Notes

- **Introspection may be disabled** in production environments for security reasons.
- If disabled, you'll need access to the **SDL (Schema Definition Language)** files directly.
- Some APIs require **authentication headers** even for introspection queries.
- Look for `kind: "INTERFACE"` in results — this distinguishes interfaces from `OBJECT`, `ENUM`, `UNION`, etc.

